# Browser
# Supportive Parents (3/3): "Tap two untapped creatures you control: Add one mana of any color." A mana ability whose two creatures are
# chosen with the activation; tapping them is not either creature's own {T}, so a summoning-sick one and Supportive Parents itself can be
# tapped. On turn 1 Bot1 taps Supportive Parents and a fresh Ornithopter (both summoning sick) for red mana and Lightning Bolts Bot2 (17).
# On turn 3 it does it again (14), then casts a second Ornithopter: with only one untapped creature of its own, though Bot2's Ornithopter
# is untapped too, the ability is not offered - it needs two of yours.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Supportive Parents
Ornithopter
Ornithopter
Lightning Bolt
Lightning Bolt
Forest
Forest x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Green)
Bot1.Hand.Supportive Parents.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter#1.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Supportive Parents.Activate(Tap: Supportive Parents; Tap: Ornithopter; Color: Red)
Bot1.Choose(Supportive Parents; Ornithopter)
? Bot1.Mana = {R}
? Client.Bot1.Mana = 1 Red
Bot1.Hand.Lightning Bolt#1.Cast(Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot2.Life = 17
? Bot1.Battlefield.Supportive Parents.Tapped = true
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Tapped = true
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Supportive Parents.Activate(Tap: Supportive Parents; Tap: Ornithopter; Color: Red)
Bot1.Choose(Supportive Parents; Ornithopter)
Bot1.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot2.Life = 14
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
! Bot1.Battlefield.Supportive Parents.Activate(Color: Red)

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter#2.Tapped = false
Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Tapped = false
